ozz-rest-pose-rotations: refuse a skeleton whose rest pose is not unit

LocalToModelJob converts each SoA block of a pose to matrices through
SoaFloat4x4::FromAffine, which asserts every lane's rotation is a unit
quaternion, the lanes past the last joint included. The rest pose a host
hands it is the skeleton's own, and Skeleton::Load took whatever rotations
the archive held: an archive aborted the host at the job, in a build with
asserts, and in one without, the job built matrices from rotations that
are no rotation.

Skeleton::Load refuses, through the archive's refusal record, a rest pose
block whose rotations are not unit by the job's own estimate.

Evidence: zozz's src/integration_test.zig loads a skeleton whose rest pose
holds a zero rotation, at a joint and in a lane no joint uses, and places
its joints; upstream aborts in FromAffine's assert, or with asserts off
loads it (measured, 2026-10-31).

diff --git a/libs/ozz/src/animation/runtime/skeleton.cc b/libs/ozz/src/animation/runtime/skeleton.cc
index 403cd60..b3324cb 100644
--- a/libs/ozz/src/animation/runtime/skeleton.cc
+++ b/libs/ozz/src/animation/runtime/skeleton.cc
@@ -210,6 +210,18 @@ void Skeleton::Load(ozz::io::IArchive& _archive, uint32_t _version) {
   }
 
   _archive >> ozz::io::MakeArray(joint_rest_poses_);
+
+  // LocalToModelJob asserts every lane of a pose it converts holds a unit
+  // rotation, padding lanes included, and a rest pose is such a pose.
+  for (size_t i = 0; i < joint_rest_poses_.size(); ++i) {
+    const math::SoaQuaternion& rotation = joint_rest_poses_[i].rotation;
+    if (!math::AreAllTrue(math::IsNormalizedEst(rotation))) {
+      _archive.Refuse("Skeleton.joint_rest_poses", static_cast<uint32_t>(i),
+                      static_cast<uint32_t>(joint_rest_poses_.size()));
+      Deallocate();
+      return;
+    }
+  }
 }
 }  // namespace animation
 }  // namespace ozz
